The Decision
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/the_villa]

FIXME(mundane): You set the journal down. You have read what you are going to read; the loose pages still in the book will not tell you anything you can use tonight. The brazier stands cold in the corner of the study, and the five ledgers are where you found them.
FIXME(mundane): Outside, Vastand is still at the gate with the two Kesharat, and perhaps an hour left to him. Whatever you mean to do with what is in this room, you do it here, before you walk back out to him.

choices:

* Carry the journal out and hand it over without a word = Let him make of it what he will
  FIXME(mundane): You come back out to the gate, careful to reach it from the road side and not the house. You give Vastand the journal whole and tell him the estate was tidy. He turns the pages slowly, the way a careful man reads, and stops a long time on the last one.
  FIXME(dread): "How much of this do you believe?" he asks, and does not wait for an answer. He puts the book inside his coat. The journal makes a kind of sense to a careful man, and you have handed him the first steps of it.
  +finish_dungeon
  +add_level

* Carry the journal out and tell Vastand what it cost = The ledgers, the cave, the girl [requires tag villa.economic_value && tag villa.danger]
  FIXME(mundane): You come back out and lay it in front of him: the formation-goods sums, the cave under the floor, the girl in the cabinet. He listens like a man doing arithmetic.
  FIXME(dread): "Formation goods," he repeats. "And a cave of them." A pause. "You understand I can't pretend I didn't hear it." He does not say whether that is a complaint or a thank-you. He is practical before he is anything else, and now he knows what it is worth and what it costs.
  +finish_dungeon
  +add_level

* Burn the journal and the ledgers in the brazier before you leave = Nothing the Kesharat can use [requires tag villa.economic_value && tag villa.danger]
  FIXME(mundane): The brazier is right here. The officials have stood outside a locked house for a day and a half and know something was worth locking, and the functionary they sent for has not arrived yet.
  @if check cunning correct:scheme wrong:hide {
    FIXME(action): You burn the journal and the marked ledgers down to ash, then come out and give Vastand a clean estate. You are both gone before the jurisdiction is decided, and the question dies on the mesa with the smell of the smoke.
    +finish_dungeon
    +add_level
    +give_gold 30
  } @else {
    FIXME(dread): You burn what you can, but the functionary arrives in time to notice the wrong things: the smell of burnt paper, the ash in the brazier, the unlocked study. Vastand will face an inquiry. You are not named in it, but the man who sent you is, and he will not forget whose hands the job was in.
    +finish_dungeon
  }

* Pocket the journal and carry only the ledgers out = You do not look too hard at why [requires tag villa.saw_cave]
  FIXME(mundane): You take the ledgers out to Vastand with a clean report and keep the journal back for yourself. Nobody finds it.
  FIXME(dread): Weeks later, on the road, you wake before dawn to find your pack reorganized. Not ransacked. Ordered, with a care you do not remember taking, and the arrangement of it is, on reflection, exactly correct. You do not mention it to anyone.
  +finish_dungeon
  +add_level
  +add_tag villa_kept_journal
